ould look like\n\nFor **EC8 / Edge Crew Quant**, the handoff should live with the project:\n\n```text\n03_PROJECTS/\n└── GCE_EC8/\n    └── GCE_EdgeCrew_Quant/\n        ├── 00_CURRENT/\n        ├── 01_HANDOFFS/\n        │   ├── ACTIVE/\n        │   └── COMPLETED/\n        ├── 02_WORK/\n        ├── 03_REGISTRY/\n        ├── 04_DECISIONS/\n        └── 90_HISTORICAL/\n```\n\nThen the actual file can retain all the routing metadata:\n\n```text\n01_HANDOFFS/\n└── ACTIVE/\n    └── 20260924-CHIAVE-TO-NICO-ECQ-VALUE-MATERIALIZATION-CONTRACT-FREEZE.md\n```\n\nInside:\n\n```yaml\nproject: GCE_EdgeCrew_Quant\nworkstream: Parent_Quant\nsender_seat: Chiave\nreceiver_seat: Nico\nhandoff_type: architecture_to_implementation\nstatus: accepted\nnext_route: Nico\nauthority: Chiave\n```\n\nNow the **artifact belongs to EC8**.\n\nChiave and Nico merely describe **who acted on it**.\n\nThat's the correct separation.\n\n---\n\n## And I'd go one step farther\n\nYour session footer is showing us that we should not have dozens of physical handoff directories by seat at all.\n\nThe filesystem can be:\n\n```text\n01_HANDOFFS/\n├── ACTIVE/\n├── CHECKPOINTS/\n├── BLOCKED/\n├── COMPLETED/\n└── SUPERSEDED/\n```\n\nAnd routing belongs in metadata:\n\n```text\nCURRENT_SEAT: Nico\nNEXT_ROUTE: Luce\nAFTER_PASS: Chiave\nFINAL_GATE: Don\nBLOCKER_ROUTE: Chiave / Don-Coda\n```\n\n**That metadata is what the carousel consumes.**\n\nSo instead of:\n\n```text\nHANDOFFS/Nico\nHANDOFFS/Luce\nHANDOFFS/Chiave\nHANDOFFS/Corrado\n```\n\nwe get:\n\n```text\nHANDOFFS/ACTIVE\n```\n\nwith a registry/index answering:\n\n```text\nWho owns it now?\nWhere is it going?\nWhat gate is it at?\n```\n\nThat's substantially cleaner.\n\n---\n\n# What stays in `GCE_ORG`\n\nThere **is** still a place for material derived from this build in ORG.\n\nFor example, if Chiave establishes a reusable architecture doctrine:\n\n```text\nGCE_ORG/\n└── Architecture/\n    ├── Current/\n    ├── Decisions/\n    ├── Standards/\n    └── Patterns/\n```\n\nBut that would contain something like:\n\n```text\nPATTERN_VALUE_MATERIALIZATION_CONTRACTS.md\n```\n\n**only after** the project result is reconciled/promoted into Framework architecture.\n\nThe actual:\n\n> “EC8 value materialization v1.0.0 — Chiave tells Nico exactly what to build”\n\nbelongs to **EC8**.\n\nThat's the Framework/project boundary working correctly.\n\n---\n\n# There's another taxonomy smell in this trace\n\nThis path:\n\n```text\nGCE_DON\\\n  GCE_EC8\\\n    GCE_EdgeCrew_Quant\\\n```\n\nis probably another piece we need to reconcile.\n\nI would **not move it blindly today**, because that is clearly the live implementation tree and we don't break working projects for aesthetic taxonomy.\n\nBut conceptually its authority is:\n\n```text\n03_PROJECTS/\n└── GCE_EC8/\n```\n\nnot **Don's personal operating surface**.\n\nSo we should classify the current local path as:\n\n**LIVE IMPLEMENTATION TRUTH — LEGACY/TRANSITIONAL LOCATION**\n\nand then decide whether:\n\n1. we physically move it later, or\n2. local runtime stays there for technical reasons while Drive/project authority points to it.\n\nThat's a reconciliation decision, **not a mass-move decision**.\n\n---\n\n## The corrected flow for the exact work you pasted\n\n```text\nEC8 / Parent Quant\n        │\n        ▼\n04_DECISIONS\nDon/Coda accepted rulings\n        │\n        ▼\nArchitecture work\nChiave freezes A–H\n        │\n        ▼\n01_HANDOFFS/ACTIVE\nChiave → Nico\n        │\n        ▼\n02_WORK\nNico implementation\n        │\n        ▼\n01_HANDOFFS/ACTIVE\nNico → Luce\n        │\n        ▼\nLuce verification\n        │\n        ▼\nChiave seam seal\n        │\n        ▼\nDon registration gate\n        │\n        ▼\n00_CURRENT\nregistered/current state\n```\n\n**One project tree. One chain.**\n\nThe seats move through it.\n\nThe artifact doesn't bounce around the enterprise taxonomy every time the seat changes.\n\n### That's the correction I would freeze\n\n> **ORG owns reusable organization