S NOT determine artifact ownership.\n\n==================================================\n2. FROZEN FRAMEWORK STATE\n==================================================\n\nDO NOT REOPEN OR RENAME THESE SEATS.\n\nDon\n- final authority / orchestrator\n\nCoda\n- strategic advisor\n- governance\n- canon\n- reconciliation\n- decision framing\n\nVittorio\n- technical advisor\n- warboard / challenge seat\n- tests premises and technical readiness\n- not implementation\n\nChiave\n- architecture seat / architecture gate\n- invoked when architecture is materially required\n\nNico\n- implementation hammer / builder\n- translates accepted architecture into working systems\n- surfaces ground-vs-spec conflicts\n\nCorrado\n- quant engine only\n- calculations, simulations, scoring, quantitative execution\n- not general architecture or implementation\n\nFalcon\n- data acquisition / retrieval\n\nTalon\n- operations / routing / coordination\n\nKeel\n- deployment / operational build support / stability\n\nLuce\n- verification / independent ground truth\n\nRagno\n- principal consultant / integration / translation when needed\n\nMagpie\n- registry / secretary\n\nPigeon\n- transport\n\nRaven\n- documentation\n\nCORE SEPARATION:\n\n    Vittorio advises.\n    Chiave architects.\n    Nico builds.\n    Corrado computes.\n    Luce verifies.\n\nMODEL != SEAT.\n\nSpace Bunny is therefore OCCUPYING LUCE.\nSpace Bunny is not a new seat.\n\n==================================================\n3. CURRENT ROOT DOCTRINE\n==================================================\n\nThe intended root separation is:\n\nGCE_ORG\n- durable organizational / governance functions\n- Framework authority surfaces\n- reusable standards / doctrine / promoted lessons\n\nGCE_IDENTITY\n- seat identities\n- AGENTS / bootstrap identity\n- seat-specific operating identity\n\nGCE_DON\n- Don's operating floor\n- command surfaces\n- temporary / live personal orchestration support\n\nPROJECTS\n- implementation truth\n- active project state\n- code\n- project artifacts\n- project-specific methodology\n- project execution\n\nFROZEN / HISTORICAL / ARCHIVE\n- provenance\n- superseded material\n- never silently promoted to current authority\n\nThese layers MUST NOT collapse into one another.\n\n==================================================\n4. FRAMEWORK VS PROJECT BOUNDARY\n==================================================\n\nFRAMEWORK OWNS:\n\n- authority\n- seat doctrine\n- canon\n- supersession\n- cross-project reconciliation\n- organizational taxonomy\n- promotion of reusable lessons\n\nPROJECTS OWN:\n\n- current implementation truth\n- code\n- active project methodology\n- build state\n- project artifacts\n- project execution\n- project-specific handoffs\n\nPROMOTION PATH:\n\nproject / experiment / POC\n    ↓\nevidence extraction\n    ↓\nreconciliation\n    ↓\nproposal\n    ↓\nFramework adoption only if accepted by Don\n\nA project artifact does NOT become a Framework artifact merely because Chiave, Nico, Luce, Corrado, etc. touched it.\n\n==================================================\n5. LIVE EVIDENCE THAT TRIGGERED THIS REVIEW\n==================================================\n\nDuring EC8 / Parent Quant work, Nico loaded cleanly from bootstrap and continued execution without manual copy/paste.\n\nExample behavior:\n\n    load Nico bootstrap\n\nNico recovered:\n\n- SEAT: Nico\n- occupant/model: Big Pickle\n- active work item\n- session ID\n- current anchor\n- Chiave architecture ruling\n- Corrado math authority\n- project implementation state\n\nNico then built:\n\n    ecq-value-materialization@1.0.0\n\nand produced a clean handoff:\n\n    Nico → Luce\n    then Chiave\n    then Don\n\nTests were green:\n    159/159\n    lint / TypeScript clean\n\nThis proves the bootstrap / seat continuity model is working well enough to expose a higher-order problem:\n\nTHE CURRENT FILESYSTEM / HANDOFF TAXONOMY IS STILL MIXING OWNERSHIP WITH ROUTING.\n\n==================================================\n6. EXAMPLE OF THE TAXONOMY DEFECT\n==================================================\n\nNico had to read a Chiave ruling from a path structurally similar to:\n\nGCE_ORG\n  \\02_COUNCILS\n    \\01_Executive_Council\n      \\Operations\n        \\06_HANDOFFS\n          \\Nico\n            \\20260924-CHIAVE-ECQ-VALUE-MATERIALIZATION-CONTRACT-FREEZE-RULING.md\n\nThis needs independent examination.\n\nPotential defects:\n\nA. EC8 project implementation handoff is stored under GCE_ORG.\n\nB. A Chiave architecture ruling is nested under Operations.\n\nC. The physical location is recipient-seat based:\n\n    06_HANDOFFS\\Nico\n\nD. Project truth lives elsewhere under:\n\n    GCE_DON\\GCE_EC8\\GCE_EdgeCrew_Quant\\...\n\nwhile governance / handoff artifacts for that same project may be scattered through GCE_ORG.\n\nE. This makes retrieval dependent on knowing:\n    who sent it,\n    who received it,\n    which old mailroom convention was used,\nrather than:\n    which project owns the work.\n\nThis is precisely the kind of ambiguity that will become dangerous if we automate carousel routing.\n\n==================================================\n7. CURRENT ARCHITECTURAL DIRECTION\n==================================================\n\nDon and Coda are converging on this principle:\n\n    ARTIFACT OWNERSHIP != ROUTING DESTINATION\n\nExample:\n\nA Chiave → Nico EC8 build contract should belong to EC8.\n\nThe file may contain:\n\n    project: GCE_EdgeCrew_Quant\n    workstream: Parent_Quant\n    sender_seat: Chiave\n    receiver_seat: Nico\n    handoff_type: architecture_to_implementation\n    status: active\n    next_route: Nico\n\nBut its physical ownership should remain with the project.\n\nPossible project pattern:\n\nPROJECT/\n  00_CURRENT/\n  01_HANDOFFS/\n      ACTIVE/\n      CHECKPOINTS/\n      BLOCKED/\n      COMPLETED/\n      SUPERSEDED/\n  02_WORK/\n  03_REGISTRY/\n  04_DECISIONS/\n  90_HISTORICAL/\n\nWe are NOT declaring this final yet.\n\nLuce must verify whether the live estate supports this direction and identify exceptions.\n\n==================================================\n8. WHY THIS MATTERS FOR THE DEV PAD CAROUSEL\n==================================================\n\nDon is reducing manual orchestration overhead.\n\nCurrent successful primitive:\n\n    load <seat> bootstrap\n\nThe same project runtime can change seat identity while maintaining project state.\n\nExample:\n\n    Nico\n      ↓\n    Luce\n      ↓\n    Chiave\n      ↓\n    Don\n\nThe desired near-term carousel is MANUAL / DON-CONTROLLED:\n\n    session footer identifies NEXT_ROUTE\n        ↓\n    DevPad highlights correct seat\n        ↓\n    Don clicks\n        ↓\n    correct bootstrap loads\n        ↓\n    work continues\n\nLater automation may advance clean high-confidence transitions, but NOT yet.\n\nBefore we automate that routing, the storage taxonomy must not teach the runtime that:\n\n    Nico owns the artifact\nor\n    Luce owns the artifact\nor\n    Operations owns every handoff.\n\nThe PROJECT owns the work.\nThe seat is the actor.\nThe footer / registry provides routing.\n\n==================================================\n9. MOBILE / CABLE CAR CONTEXT\n==================================================\n\nDo not over-design this section.\n\nThe larger operating model now emerging is:\n\nDON INPUT\n    ↓\nvoice / idea / approval / decision\n    ↓\nexecutor\n    ↓\nclassification\n    ↓\nnormalizer / compiler\n    ↓\nproject/workstream routing\n    ↓\nisolated DevPad runtime\n    ↓\nseat/bootstrap carousel\n    ↓\nCable Car persistence / handoff\n    ↓\nnext seat / next gate\n\nPhone is NOT intended to be a second full Command Center.\n\nPhone is primarily:\n\n- approve\n- hold\n- defer\n- open context\n- redirect\n- escalate\n\nThe goal is mobile exception orchestration, not mobile development.\n\nThis taxonomy review therefore matters because Google Drive / Cable Car may become the durable handoff/persistence plane for these flows.\n\n==================================================\n10. WHAT NICO ALREADY DID\n==================================================\n\nNico has already used multiple agents to inspect the implementation and relevant surfaces.\n\nTreat Nico's recon as BUILDER-SIDE EVIDENCE.\n\nDo not assume it is automatically correct.\n\nBut do not waste time reproducing obvious facts simply to say Luce independently looked at them.\n\nUse Luce independence where it matters:\n\n- path reality\n- ownership reality\n- duplicate authority\n- stale routing structures\n- project/framework boundary violations\n- current-vs-historical ambiguity\n- risks to carousel automation\n- risks to Cable Car retrieval\n\n==================================================\n11. LUCE'S REQUIRED QUESTIONS\n==================================================\n\nFor every relevant live surface, determine:\n\nPATH:\nCURRENT FUNCTION:\nACTUAL CONTENT OWNER:\nCURRENT AUTHORITY:\nLIVE / SUPPORTING / HISTORICAL:\nPROJECT-SPECIFIC OR FRAMEWORK-GENERAL:\nROUTING-COUPLED NAME? YES/NO:\nDUPLICATE AUTHORITY? YES/NO:\nKEEP / RENAME / MOVE / SUPERSEDE / ARCHIVE / UNKNOWN:\nRISK IF LEFT AS-IS:\n\nPay special attention to:\n\n1. GCE_ORG handoff trees\n2. Operations handoff/mailroom structures\n3. seat-named recipient directories\n4. EC8 / Edge Crew Quant project truth\n5. GCE_DON project placement\n6. GCE_IDENTITY\n7. Cable Car handoff paths\n8. current Framework surfaces\n9. current Google Drive taxonomy\n10. historical/frozen material\n\n==================================================\n12. REQUIRED CLASSIFICATION RULES\n==================================================\n\nKEEP when:\n- path represents a durable function\n- authority is clear\n- no duplicate live authority\n- placement is coherent\n\nRENAME when:\n- live name materially misstates function or authority\n- retired routing/seat coupling causes confusion\n\nMOVE when:\n- artifact clearly belongs to another authority domain\n- current placement creates retrieval/routing ambiguity\n\nSUPERSEDE when:\n- useful history remains\n- but artifact must not present as current\n\nARCHIVE when:\n- historical/provenance only\n- no longer belongs on live surface\n\nDO NOT CHANGE when:\n- historical naming is accurate\n- provenance requires original name\n- issue is merely aesthetic\n\nUNKNOWN when:\n- evidence is insufficient\n- do not infer\n\n==================================================\n13. IMPORTANT HYPOTHESIS TO TEST\n==================================================\n\nThe current working hypothesis from Don/Coda is:\n\n    GCE_ORG should NOT be the project handoff mailroom.\n\n    PROJECT should own project-specific handoffs.\n\n    GCE_IDENTITY should hold seat identity/bootstrap material.\n\n    Routing should be metadata / registry / runtime state.\n\n    Seat-specific folders should not determine artifact ownership.\n\n    Operations may own routing SYSTEMS and routing POLICY,\n    but should not automatically own every artifact being routed.\n\nLuce must VERIFY this against ground truth.\n\nDo not merely agree.\n\n==================================================\n14. GOOGLE DRIVE TARGET PRINCIPLE\n==================================================\n\nGoogle Drive should mimic the AUTHORITY / ROUTING MODEL,\nnot blindly clone every local filesystem detail.\n\nDrive should make it possible for a fresh session to answer:\n\n- What project owns this?\n- What is current?\n- What is historical?\n- What decision governs this?\n- Which seat currently acts?\n- Who acts next?\n- Where is implementation truth?\n- Where is Framework authority?\n- What is superseded?\n- Where does the next handoff go?\n\nwithout guessing from filenames.\n\nGOOGLE DRIVE REMAINS READ-ONLY UNTIL DON ACCEPTS THE PLAN.\n\n==================================================\n15. REQUIRED DELIVERABLE\n==================================================\n\nReturn ONE reconciliation package.\n\nA. EXECUTIVE FINDING\n- Is the taxonomy materially wrong?\n- Where exactly?\n- How severe is it?\n- What is safe to leave alone?\n\nB. CURRENT PATH MAP\nFor each important live path:\n- function\n- owner\n- authority\n- classification\n- disposition\n\nC. CONFIRMED TAXONOMY DEFECTS\nSeparate:\n- real authority defect\n- routing/storage coupling\n- stale naming only\n- harmless aesthetics\n\nD. PROJECT/HANDOFF OWNERSHIP RULING\nDetermine whether project-specific handoffs should live under project roots rather than GCE_ORG/Operations/seat mailrooms.\n\nE. GCE_ORG TREATMENT\nState what belongs there and what does not.\n\nF. GCE_IDENTITY TREATMENT\nConfirm identity/bootstrap role.\n\nG. GCE_DON TREATMENT\nIdentify project trees currently living under GCE_DON and classify whether:\n- correct permanent location\n- transitional legacy location\n- move later\n- leave physically but pointer elsewhere\n\nDO NOT MOVE THEM.\n\nH. CAROUSEL READINESS\nState what taxonomy corrections are required BEFORE routing automation can safely consume NEXT_ROUTE / gate metadata.\n\nI. CABLE CAR / DRIVE READINESS\nState what needs to change for reliable project-owned handoff persistence.\n\nJ. KEEP LIST\n\nK. RENAME LIST\n\nL. MOVE LIST\nPLAN ONLY\n\nM. SUPERSEDE LIST\n\nN. ARCHIVE LIST\n\nO. UNKNOWN / DON DECISIONS REQUIRED\n\nP. SURGICAL EXECUTION PLAN\nSmallest safe sequence.\nNo mass reorganization.\n\n==================================================\n16. STOP CONDITIONS\n==================================================\n\nSTOP and route to Don/Coda if you find:\n\n- two competing current authority surfaces\n- project truth that cannot be safely assigned\n- current production tooling hard-coded to the old paths\n- taxonomy changes that would break bootstrap loading\n- Cable Car depending on recipient-seat folder names\n- any move that would invalidate active EC8 work\n- ambiguity between historical and current Framework doctrine\n\nDo NOT resolve those silently.\n\n==================================================\n17. NON-NEGO