r enough state to continue work.\n\nThe near-term target is:\n\n    project runtime\n        ↓\n    current seat\n        ↓\n    machine-readable footer\n        ↓\n    NEXT_ROUTE\n        ↓\n    DevPad highlights next seat\n        ↓\n    Don clicks once\n        ↓\n    load <next-seat> bootstrap\n        ↓\n    continue\n\nNO full autonomous carousel yet.\n\nDon remains the orchestrator.\n\nThe purpose of this pass is to make the underlying control plane trustworthy enough that the click-carousel can be built on it without encoding the current filesystem/routing mistakes.\n\n==================================================\n2. VERIFIED LUCE FINDINGS — ACCEPT AS GROUND TRUTH INPUT\n==================================================\n\nLuce / Space Bunny independently established:\n\nA. CURRENT CANON IS STALE / COMPETING\n- current canonical surfaces still name retired/model identities incorrectly.\n- an un-deny-listed competing bootstrap exists under GCE_DON\\03_HANDOFFS\\handoff\\AGENTS.md.\n\nB. ROUTING IS FRAGMENTED\nThere are multiple live handoff/routing buses with incompatible rosters:\n- Operations\\06_HANDOFFS\n- ai-inbox\n- mailroom\\seats\n- GCE_DON\\03_HANDOFFS\\handoff\nand related routing residue.\n\nC. IDENTITY IS POLLUTED\nRuntime cwd currently roots seats at:\n    GCE_IDENTITY\\<Seat>\n\nThis has caused work product to accumulate in identity directories.\n\nIdentity must remain bootstrap/load-control, not become project working storage.\n\nD. PROJECT OWNERSHIP PRINCIPLE IS VALID\nGCE_ORG\\04_PROJECTS is already a compliant pointer/index layer.\n\nProject-scoped artifacts belong with the project.\nFramework-general artifacts belong in GCE_ORG.\nRouting destination does NOT determine artifact ownership.\n\nE. NEXT_ROUTE IS NOT MACHINE SAFE\nNEXT_ROUTE exists widely as free text.\nThere is no stable machine-readable footer schema / validator carrying:\n- project\n- workstream\n- current seat\n- next route\n- gate\n- confidence\n- blocker route\n\nF. CABLE CAR CONTRACT IS TOO NARROW\nCurrent contract:\n- hardcodes project = GCE_Stack\n- authority enum is too narrow and has already caused false attribution\n- rejects required routing metadata\n- is filename-addressed\n- must be corrected BEFORE Drive integration hardens\n\nG. MANUAL CAROUSEL IS CONDITIONALLY READY\nAutomated carousel is not.\n\nLuce specifically found:\n- board does not cover all required seats\n- no Corrado tile\n- panes have no project/workstream/gate dimension\n- NEXT_ROUTE is free text\n\nH. ACTIVE EC8 MUST NOT BE MOVED\nEC8 / Edge Crew Quant physical implementation is coherent and live.\nDo not destabilize it in this pass.\n\n==================================================\n3. PRIMARY PASS OBJECTIVE\n==================================================\n\nAt completion, the following must be true:\n\n1. ONE authoritative current bootstrap/routing authority exists.\n2. Known competing stale bootstrap cannot silently launch.\n3. Seat identity directories no longer receive normal project work product.\n4. A machine-readable session/footer routing contract exists.\n5. The DevPad runtime can identify:\n       PROJECT\n       WORKSTREAM\n       CURRENT_SEAT\n       NEXT_ROUTE\n       GATE\n       CONFIDENCE\n       BLOCKER_ROUTE\n6. The seat registry / board supports the frozen active roster required for routing.\n7. Cable Car contract can carry arbitrary project/workstream/routing information without false authority attribution.\n8. Existing live project paths continue working.\n9. No historical provenance is rewritten.\n10. No Google Drive writes occur.\n11. No mass filesystem migration occurs.\n12. The result is immediately usable as the substrate for:\n       click seat → load bootstrap → continue.\n\n==================================================\n4. USE SUB-AGENTS\n==================================================\n\nNico owns the build.\n\nLaunch parallel sub-agents to inspect / implement bounded pieces where useful.\n\nSuggested lane