y current Don ruling.\nTreat any live Ragno references as stale current-state residue unless explicitly historical.\n\nMODEL != SEAT.\n\nBig Pickle, Space Bunny, GLM, Kimi, etc. are occupants/providers/models, not seats.\n\n==================================================\n3. CORE DOCTRINE\n==================================================\n\nFramework continuity must NOT depend on model memory or model consistency.\n\nThe deterministic chain should be:\n\n    authoritative registry\n        ↓\n    seat/bootstrap\n        ↓\n    project state\n        ↓\n    machine-readable routing/control metadata\n        ↓\n    runtime/model occupant\n\nModels execute.\nFramework carries continuity.\n\n==================================================\n4. ROOT OWNERSHIP MODEL\n==================================================\n\nReconcile against this intended separation:\n\nGCE_ORG\n- durable Framework authority\n- governance\n- doctrine\n- taxonomy\n- routing policy/schemas\n- promotion/supersession\n- pointer/index surfaces\n\nGCE_IDENTITY\n- live seat identity\n- AGENTS/bootstrap/load control\n- no routine project work product\n\nGCE_DON\n- Don's operating floor\n- command surfaces\n- working support surfaces\n\nPROJECT ROOTS\n- implementation truth\n- project-specific artifacts\n- active project state\n- project-specific handoffs\n- project methodology\n- project execution\n\nARCHIVE / FROZEN / HISTORICAL\n- provenance\n- superseded state\n- never silently current\n\nROUTING / TRANSPORT\n- metadata\n- queues\n- hints\n- delivery\n- does NOT determine artifact ownership\n\n==================================================\n5. KNOWN PRIOR LUCE FINDINGS TO RECHECK\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT assume these are still true.\nVerify whether each is:\n    STILL TRUE\n    FIXED\n    PARTIALLY FIXED\n    SUPERSEDED\n    UNKNOWN\n\nPrior findings included:\n\nA. stale canonical README / roster\n- Big Pickle represented as identity\n- Kimi represented as current\n- stale roster doctrine\n\nB. multiple routing/handoff buses\n- Operations\\06_HANDOFFS\n- ai-inbox\n- mailroom\\seats\n- GCE_DON\\03_HANDOFFS\\handoff\n- possibly others\n\nC. identity pollution\n- seat cwd rooted into GCE_IDENTITY\\<Seat>\n- work product accumulating inside identity directories\n\nD. stale/competing bootstrap\n- GCE_DON\\03_HANDOFFS\\handoff\\AGENTS.md\n- old GLM/Kimi-era routing\n- Don referred to as \"Dekan\"\n\nE. Cable Car contract mismatch\n- hard-coded project\n- narrow authority enum\n- false attribution\n- insufficient metadata support\n- filename-addressed behavior\n\nF. root authorization registry drift\n- pending / stale registration model\n- unregistered live surfaces\n\nG. 06_HANDOFFS overloading\n- recipient-seat mailbox acting as de facto artifact home\n\nH. project-specific artifacts living outside project roots\n\nI. stale shared-state / T1 / council identity residue\n\nJ. four-or-more roster copies disagreeing\n\nK. stale/dead seat references\n- specifically Ragno now known RETIRED by Don ruling\n\n==================================================\n6. SPECIAL FOCUS: LIVE BOOTSTRAPS\n==================================================\n\nThis is now a major concern.\n\nInspect EVERY currently live seat bootstrap / AGENTS surface.\n\nFor each active seat determine:\n\nSEAT:\nBOOTSTRAP PATH:\nACTIVE IN REGISTRY?:\nROUTABLE?:\nROLE TEXT CURRENT?:\nDEAD-SEAT REFERENCES?:\nMODEL-AS-SEAT REFERENCES?:\nOLD DEPARTMENT / COUNCIL REFERENCES?:\nSTALE TALON/KEEL/RAGNO/KIMI/CALIBRO REFERENCES?:\nUSES ONE CURRENT AUTHORITY SOURCE?:\nCURRENT / STALE / CONFLICTED:\n\nWe already observed Nico booting with stale content including:\n\n    Ragno is on-demand, not a gate.\n\nThat is now wrong because Ragno is retired.\n\nAlso inspect whether live bootstraps still emit obsolete fields such as:\n\n    class UNSET\n    rank UNSET\n    animal UNSET\n\nDetermine whether those fields are:\n- current schema\n- legacy schema\n- harmless display residue\n- dangerous authority residue\n\nDo not guess.\n\n==================================================\n7. SPECIAL FOCUS: AUTHORITATIVE ROSTER\n==================================================\n\nFind every place that currently declares or implies the live seat roster.\n\nFor each source:\n\nPATH:\nROSTER:\nCLAIMED AUTHORITY:\nACTUALLY CONSUMED BY RUNTIME?:\nCURRENT / STALE / HISTORICAL:\nCONFLICTS WITH DON RULING?:\n\nWe need to know which roster source actually controls:\n- bootstrap resolution\n- DevPad seat resolution\n- routing\n- Cable Car\n- mailroom / inbox\n- any registry\n- current Framework docs\n\nGoal is NOT to fix during recon.\nGoal is to identify the one source that SHOULD become authoritative and every source that must become pointer/history/superseded.\n\n==================================================\n8. SPECIAL FOCUS: PROJECT OWNERSHIP\n==================================================\n\nVerify this principle against current disk:\n\n    project-scoped artifact → project root\n    Framework-general artifact → GCE_ORG\n    identity artifact → GCE_IDENTITY\n    routing metadata → routing/registry/transport\n    destination seat != artifact owner\n\nInspect especially:\n\n- EC8 / Edge Crew Quant\n- GCE Stack\n- Framework Reconciliation\n- VoiceBridge\n- any current project handoffs living under GCE_ORG/Operations/seat folders\n\nFor project-specific artifacts currently outside project roots, classify:\n\nCORRECT TO MOVE LATER\nPOINTER ONLY\nHISTORICAL\nCURRENT BUT TRANSITIONAL\nBLOCKED\nUNKNOWN\n\nDo NOT move anything in this pass.\n\n==================================================\n9. SPECIAL FOCUS: ROUTING / BUS REALITY\n==================================================\n\nEnumerate every currently active routing / handoff / mailbox / inbox mechanism.\n\nFor each:\n\nPATH / SYSTEM:\nLIVE?:\nCONSUMER:\nPRODUCER:\nROSTER SOURCE:\nPROJECT-AWARE?:\nSEAT-AWARE?:\nMODEL-COUPLED?:\nAUTHORITATIVE OR TRANSPORT ONLY?:\nCURRENT DEPENDEN