": []}, {"message_id": "79359c71-d993-45c7-83f8-bb0762086819", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790380887.0014, "updated_at": 1790380888.207926, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Okay. Here's the rebuild. Session header is timestamp, authority, seat plus occupant, mode, thread name, context in one", "text_chars": 120, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "c6e5aff6-f248-44a3-b399-66758f132234", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790380889.795733, "updated_at": 1790380936.540537, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Okay, so do me a favor, do the rebuild and show me the rebuild.", "text_chars": 63, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "623e57c1-7062-4678-ad5a-464107047ef0", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790380892.110374, "updated_at": 1790380892.110374, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "model_editable_context", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "66e16803-2451-4d24-8adb-d5588d161510", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790380898.070537, "updated_at": 1790380898.070537, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "016f01bf-ac06-4af4-9a26-65b8c7862cd1", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790380898.073362, "updated_at": 1790380935.715211, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yes. Here’s the **rebuilt version** I’d standardize around. The key change is that the **core header and footer stay small**, while everything that can drift or multiply lives in explicit appendices.\n\n# GCE SESSION HEADER — CORE\n\n```text\nGCE SESSION HEADER\n\nTIMESTAMP:            2026-09-25 16:56 PT\nAUTHORITY:            Don\nPRIMARY SEAT:         Coda\nOCCUPANT / MODEL:     GPT-5.6 Sol\nMODE:                 Reconciliation\nCURRENT THREAD:       Framework Taxonomy / Routing Reconciliation\nCURRENT CONTEXT:      Reconcile live machine state against frozen Framework authority,\n                      then prepare the bounded Nico correction package.\nMATURITY:             POC | DEVELOPMENT | VALIDATION | PRODUCTION-READY | PRODUCTION\nSTATUS:               ACTIVE\nCONFIDENCE:           97%\nCURRENT ANCHOR:       <current authoritative artifact / ruling / handoff>\n```\n\nThat is the **orientation block**.\n\nThe important distinctions are now explicit:\n\n- **MODE** = what kind of work we are doing: `RECONCILIATION`, `IMPLEMENTATION`, `VERIFICATION`, `ARCHITECTURE`, etc.\n- **CURRENT THREAD** = the named thing we are talking about.\n- **CURRENT CONTEXT** = one or two sentences explaining where we are inside that thread.\n- **MATURITY** = how mature the thing is.\n- **STATUS** = what the session itself is doing.\n- **CONFIDENCE** = current confidence in the active frame/state.\n\n---\n\n# SESSION HEADER APPENDIX — ACTIVE CONTEXT BOARD\n\nThis sits **immediately underneath the header**.\n\n```text\nACTIVE CONTEXT APPENDIX\n\nPROMOTED / CURRENT:\n  Framework Taxonomy / Routing Reconciliation\n\nPARKED IN THIS THREAD:\n  1. Cable Car / Google Drive handoff transport\n     State: functional transport; schema/taxonomy reconciliation pending\n\n  2. Session Controller / Carousel\n     State: concept accepted; implementation intentionally deferred\n\n  3. Open Handoff utility\n     State: Nico implementation spec prepared\n\n  4. Mobile Orchestration / Vomit Runtime\n     State: architectural concept; not current implementation lane\n```\n\nThis is the piece I think is going to help us enormously.\n\nWhen you say:\n\n> “Hold taxonomy. Let’s work on Cable Car.”\n\nwe do **not** rewrite the whole session.\n\nWe simply promote:\n\n```text\nPROMOTED / CURRENT:\n  Cable Car / Google Drive handoff transport\n\nPARKED:\n  Framework Taxonomy / Routing Reconciliation\n  Session Controller / Carousel\n  Open Handoff utility\n```\n\nNow both of us know exactly which conversation inside the conversation is active.\n\nNo silent context hopping.\n\n---\n\n# CORE SESSION FOOTER\n\nMuch smaller than what I was using before:\n\n```text\nGCE SESSION FOOTER\n\nSEAT:                 Coda\nSESSION STATUS:       CHECKPOINT\nOUTCOME:              <what materially happened>\nCONFIDENCE:           97%\n\nDECISIONS:\n- <accepted decision>\n- <accepted decision>\n\nBLOCKERS:\n- <only actual blocker>\n\nOPEN ITEMS:\n- <unfinished item>\n\nNEXT ROUTE:           Nico\nNEXT ACTION:          <precise next action>\n\nHANDOFF:              <handoff artifact id/path if one exists>\n```\n\nThat's enough.\n\nWe **do not** shove Cable Car status, controller status, every project state, Drive status, identity state, taxonomy state, etc. into the core footer.\n\nThe footer should answer:\n\n> **What just happened, how sure are we, what's unresolved, and where does it go?**\n\n---\n\n# FOOTER APPENDIX — ROUTING / HANDOFF PACKET\n\nThen comes the machine-useful stuff.\n\nThis is where I would put the data that eventually feeds Carousel, Cable Car, Drive, OpenCode, etc.\n\n```text\nROUTING / HANDOFF APPENDIX\n\nPROJECT:              GCE_Framework\nWORKSTREAM:           Taxonomy_Reconciliation\nSESSION_ID:           20260925-CODA-001\n\nCURRENT_SEAT:         Coda\nNEXT_ROUTE:           Nico\nAFTER_PASS:           Luce\nFINAL_GATE:           Don\n\nGATE:                 implementation\nBLOCKER_ROUTE:        Don/Coda\nCURRENT_ANCHOR:       <artifact-id-or-path>\n\nHANDOFF_ID:           <stable handoff id>\nHANDOFF_TYPE:         governance_to_implementation\n\nLOCAL_HANDOFF_PATH:\nC:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\...\\20260925-CODA-TO-NICO.md\n\nDRIVE_HANDOFF:\n<Google Drive URL once Cable Car publishes it>\n\nLOCAL_OPEN:\n<local actionable/open reference once implemented>\n\nDRIVE_ARTIFACT_ID:\n<Drive file ID if available>\n\nCABLE_CAR_STATE:\nPUBLISHED | QUEUED | RECEIVED | NONE\n```\n\nNow we're separating **human session state** from **machine routing state**.\n\nThat's the right boundary.\n\n---\n\n# The handoff itself\n\nEvery real handoff should eventually give you **both sides**:\n\n### Human / cloud copy\n\n```text\nOPEN IN GOOGLE DRIVE:\n[HANDOFF]\n```\n\nThat points to the persistent copy Cable Car published.\n\n### Machine / local copy\n\n```text\nOPEN LOCAL HANDOFF:\nC:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\GCE_DON\\...\\handoff.md\n```\n\nAnd eventually the DevPad/OpenCode surface can render:\n\n```text\n[ OPEN LOCAL ]    [ OPEN DRIVE ]\n```\n\nThose are two representations of the **same handoff ID**.\n\nThat's important.\n\nWe should **not** have “the local handoff” and “the Drive handoff” as conceptually different artifacts.\n\nIt should be:\n\n```text\nHANDOFF_ID\n    │\n    ├── LOCAL_PATH\n    └── DRIVE_ARTIFACT_ID / DRIVE_URL\n```\n\nSo Cable Car is transport/persistence, not an artifact duplication model.\n\n---\n\n# Full assembled example\n\nHere's what I think an actual session should look like:\n\n```text\n==================================================\nGCE SESSION HEADER\n==================================================\n\nTIMESTAMP:            2026-09-25 16:56 PT\nAUTHORITY:            Don\nPRIMARY SEAT:         Coda\nOCCUPANT / MODEL:     GPT-5.6 Sol\nMODE:                 RECONCILIATION\nCURRENT THREAD:       Framework Taxonomy / Routing Reconciliation\nCURRENT CONTEXT:      Reconciling live machine state against frozen Framework\n                      authority before the Nico implementation pass.\nMATURITY:             DEVELOPMENT\nSTATUS:               ACTIVE\nCONFIDENCE:           97%\nCURRENT ANCHOR:       Luce current-state reconciliation\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nACTIVE CONTEXT APPENDIX\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nPROMOTED / CURRENT:\n- Framework Taxonomy / Routing Reconciliation\n\nPARKED:\n- Cable Car / Drive transport\n- Session Controller / Carousel\n- Open Handoff utility\n- Mobile Orchestration / Vomit Runtime\n\n==================================================\n... SESSION WORK ...\n==================================================\n\n==================================================\nGCE SESSION FOOTER\n==================================================\n\nSEAT:                 Coda\nSESSION STATUS:       CHECKPOINT\nOUTCOME:              Reconciliation accepted and bounded Nico package prepared.\nCONFIDENCE:           97%\n\nDECISIONS:\n- Project owns project-specific artifacts.\n- Routing destination does not determine artifact ownership.\n\nBLOCKERS:\n- Current machine reconciliation must complete before execution.\n\nOPEN ITEMS:\n- Reconcile live roster/bootstrap residue.\n\nNEXT ROUTE:           Nico\nNEXT ACTION:          Execute accepted correction package.\n\nHANDOFF:              GCE-HO-20260925-0042\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nROUTING / HANDOFF APPENDIX\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nPROJECT:              GCE_Framework\nWORKSTREAM:           Taxonomy_Reconciliation\nSESSION_ID:           20260925-CODA-001\n\nCURRENT_SEAT:         Coda\nNEXT_ROUTE:           Nico\nAFTER_PASS:           Luce\nFINAL_GATE:           Don\n\nGATE:                 implementation\nBLOCKER_ROUTE:        Don/Coda\n\nHANDOFF_ID:           GCE-HO-20260925-0042\nHANDOFF_TYPE:         governance_to_implementation\n\nLOCAL_HANDOFF_PATH:\nC:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\...\\20260925-CODA-TO-NICO.md\n\nDRIVE_HANDOFF_URL:\n<published URL>\n\nDRIVE_ARTIFACT_ID:\n<Drive ID>\n\nCABLE_CAR_STATE:      PUBLISHED\n```\n\n## One more thing I would freeze\n\n**Promotion is explicit.**\n\nWhenever we change subjects inside a long-running chat, we update only:\n\n```text\nCURRENT THREAD\nCURRENT CONTEXT\nPROMOTED / CURRENT\nPARKED\n```\n\nEverything else keeps its identity.\n\nThat gives us exactly what you're after: **you and I can bounce between three or four workstreams without the session itself losing its operating frame.**\n\nAnd the **handoff appendix becomes the bridge to Cable Car/OpenCode**, rather than bloating the human-readable footer.", "text_chars": 8227, "code_blocks": 11, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": ["Brother\\...\\20260925-CODA-TO-NICO.md", "Brother\\GCE_DON\\...\\handoff.md", "C:\\Users\\Dekan"], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "2d3671fa-50e2-4f55-b8a9-9e1af9149496", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790380938.2117, "updated_at": 1790380958.098879, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "One addition. I want to do a days running. I want to do a days running for that. Whatever we're doing, you should be smart enough to calculate the days of when it started versus the days active versus the days whatever. See what I'm saying? That's overall. We don't have to do it by what it's promoted. Just overall days running. So we're going to start working in KPIs.", "text_chars": 370, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "41ef0cfe-8c6b-47d0-964a-1f0554aaa91d", "role": "system", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790380941.234168, "updated_at": 1790380941.234168, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 0, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "7153a48a-c1f8-4877-b5fa-0746f8da9624", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790380942.234425, "updated_at": 1790380942.234425, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "f95cef02-66e8-4a68-a488-67b1dbe4ddab", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790380942.237699, "updated_at": 1790380957.366065, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yes. **That belongs in the core header**, because it describes the lifecycle of the overall thread/workstream, not whichever item happens to be promoted today.\n\nAnd I like where you're going with it: this becomes the first piece of **session/workstream KPIs**.\n\nI would add a compact lifecycle block:\n\n```text\nSTARTED:              2026-09-23 15:59 PT\nDAYS RUNNING:         3\nACTIVE DAYS:          3\nLAST ACTIVE:          2026-09-25 16:56 PT\n```\n\nBut I want the semantics deterministic:\n\n- **STARTED** = timestamp the overall thread/workstream was established.\n- **DAYS RUNNING** = calendar days from `STARTED` through now, inclusive. This keeps it human-readable: started Wednesday, working Friday = Day 3.\n- **ACTIVE DAYS** = distinct calendar days on which the thread actually had recorded activity.\n- **LAST ACTIVE** = latest recorded activity timestamp.\n\nLater we can add deeper KPIs without bloating the header: elapsed hours, active work hours, number of handoffs, seat transitions, gates passed, blockers, rework loops, average confidence, etc. Those belong in a **KPI appendix**, not the core header.\n\nSo the revised header becomes:\n\n```text\n==================================================\nGCE SESSION HEADER\n==================================================\n\nTIMESTAMP:            2026-09-25 16:56 PT\nAUTHORITY:            Don\nPRIMARY SEAT:         Coda\nOCCUPANT / MODEL:     GPT-5.6 Sol\n\nMODE:                 RECONCILIATION\nCURRENT THREAD:       Framework Taxonomy / Routing Reconciliation\nCURRENT CONTEXT:      Reconciling live machine state against frozen\n                      Framework authority before implementation.\n\nMATURITY:             DEVELOPMENT\nSTATUS:               ACTIVE\nCONFIDENCE:           97%\n\nSTARTED:              <original thread/workstream timestamp>\nDAYS RUNNING:         <calculated automatically>\nACTIVE DAYS:          <calculated from recorded activity>\nLAST ACTIVE:          <latest activity timestamp>\n\nCURRENT ANCHOR:       <current authoritative artifact>\n```\n\nThen below it remains:\n\n```text\n--------------------------------------------------\nACTIVE CONTEXT APPENDIX\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nPROMOTED / CURRENT:\n- Taxonomy / Routing Reconciliation\n\nPARKED:\n- Cable Car\n- Session Controller / Carousel\n- Open Handoff\n- Mobile Orchestration\n```\n\n### And here's the important design rule\n\n**Promotion does not reset the clock.**\n\nIf we spend Monday on taxonomy, Tuesday on Cable Car, Wednesday back on taxonomy, this is still the same overall thread:\n\n```text\nSTARTED:       Monday\nDAYS RUNNING:  3\nACTIVE DAYS:   3\n```\n\nThe promoted item changes. The lifecycle doesn't.\n\nThat gives us the beginnings of actual operational telemetry instead of vibes about how long something has been going.\n\nEventually we should be able to say:\n\n> **Project has been running 11 days, 7 active days, 18 handoffs, 4 gates, 2 blockers, 1 rework loop, 96% current confidence.**\n\nNow we're starting to measure the Framework itself.", "text_chars": 2983, "code_blocks": 4, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "c66c509f-db6f-479d-b890-b687894e335f", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790380969.5418, "updated_at": 1790380983.543158, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Also in the header, I want priority: high, medium, low. That's all we need, high, medium, low. Right? So right now the dev pad is high priority. Something like Voice Bridge tweaks is low priority. Session controller, high, medium priority. Right?", "text_chars": 246, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "2ed315d9-af89-4063-9015-06d666a9553c", "role": "system", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790380972.865583, "updated_at": 1790380972.865583, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 0, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "1d4a50dc-5c8a-4cc4-8d40-74d661719bd8", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790380972.889518, "updated_at": 1790382709.556593, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yes. **Priority belongs in the core header** because it tells the whole team how much attention/resources the current thread deserves.\n\nAnd keep it deliberately simple:\n\n**HIGH · MEDIUM · LOW**\n\nNo P0/P1/P2, no five-level scoring system.\n\nI’d put it beside maturity/status:\n\n```text\n==================================================\nGCE SESSION HEADER\n==================================================\n\nTIMESTAMP:            2026-09-25 16:56 PT\nAUTHORITY:            Don\nPRIMARY SEAT:         Coda\nOCCUPANT / MODEL:     GPT-5.6 Sol\n\nMODE:                 RECONCILIATION\nCURRENT THREAD:       Framework Taxonomy / Routing Reconciliation\nCURRENT CONTEXT:      Reconciling live machine state against frozen\n                      Framework authority before implementation.\n\nPRIORITY:             HIGH\nMATURITY:             DEVELOPMENT\nSTATUS:               ACTIVE\nCONFIDENCE:           97%\n\nSTARTED:              <original start timestamp>\nDAYS RUNNING:         <automatic>\nACTIVE DAYS:          <automatic>\nLAST ACTIVE:          <automatic>\n\nCURRENT ANCHOR:       <current authoritative artifact>\n```\n\nAnd I’d define the priority semantics tightly:\n\n- **HIGH** — central build, active blocker, production-critical, or something Don is actively driving. **Main DevPad** is a good example.\n- **MEDIUM** — important enabling work, but it doesn't displace the primary build. **Session Controller/Carousel** could sit here while DevPad is the active high-priority work.\n- **LOW** — worthwhile improvement/tweak that can wait without materially blocking the estate. **VoiceBridge polish/tweaks** is the right example.\n\nThe useful future behavior is that **priority becomes routable metadata**, too. If five parked threads exist, the Framework doesn't have to guess what Don cares about:\n\n```text\nHIGH     DevPad\nMEDIUM   Session Controller\nLOW      VoiceBridge tweaks\n```\n\nThen when we start building the KPI layer, we can measure things like **days running by priority, aging high-priority work, high-priority blockers, and time spent on low-priority work while high-priority work remains blocked.**\n\nThat's operationally useful without making the header complicated.", "text_chars": 2161, "code_blocks": 2, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "13a420eb-73b7-4958-bc31-3fae203c146b", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790381015.52769, "updated_at": 1790381029.251282, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Last thing I want is put a placeholder for basically when I do voice to text, I want a placeholder in the session header that says basically what I said in two lines. I want to see how you interpret it with my intent and objective. So basically you're making an appendix to the session header now, two, three lines, my intent, objective, and context.", "text_chars": 350, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "919fea18-0511-44b1-9f6b-6a627bcdbfc4", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790381019.996262, "updated_at": 1790381029.142904, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yes. That belongs in a **header appendix**, not the core header.\n\nI’d make it a compact **Don Intent Snapshot** so every session starts with both the machine frame and my interpretation of what you actually meant.\n\n```text\n--------------------------------------------------\nDON INTENT SNAPSHOT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nRAW INTENT:\n<1–2 line plain-language summary of what Don just said>\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n<what outcome Don is actually trying to achieve>\n\nCONTEXT:\n<why this matters / what surrounding constraint or situation applies>\n```\n\nFor example, from what you just said:\n\n```text\nDON INTENT SNAPSHOT\n\nRAW INTENT:\nDon wants every voice-to-text input reduced to a short, visible interpretation\nso he can immediately validate whether the session understood him correctly.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\nExpose intent before execution so misunderstandings are caught early\nwithout forcing Don to rewrite or formalize his raw voice input.\n\nCONTEXT:\nThis is especially important in long-running sessions with multiple promoted\nand parked workstreams, where raw voice input may jump context quickly.\n```\n\nAnd I’d add one rule: **this block is interpretive, not authoritative.**\n\nIf you say, “No, that’s not what I meant,” we correct the snapshot immediately. It should never silently become canon just because I summarized you.\n\nSo the header stack is now:\n\n```text\nGCE SESSION HEADER\n- timestamp\n- authority\n- primary seat\n- occupant/model\n- mode\n- current thread\n- current context\n- priority\n- maturity\n- status\n- confidence\n- started\n- days running\n- active days\n- last active\n- current anchor\n\nHEADER APPENDIX A — DON INTENT SNAPSHOT\n- raw intent\n- objective\n- context\n\nHEADER APPENDIX B — ACTIVE CONTEXT BOARD\n- promoted/current\n- parked\n```\n\nThat gives you a really nice visual check at the top of every session:\n\n**What are we doing? Why are we doing it? Did the system understand me? What else is parked?**", "text_chars": 1915, "code_blocks": 3, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "7f6969b0-7383-4e5b-a3e1-b3610325807d", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790381052.3902001, "updated_at": 1790381105.728636, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Perfect. Build it out. Perfect. Build it out. That's the version two, I would say. Maybe even version three. We'll say version three of the session header and session footer. So build it out first. I think, and update it, right? And then we're gonna drop an anchor first, and then we'll do something else.", "text_chars": 305, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "7b306781-2fe9-4586-b473-db760fe97c20", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790381062.776576, "updated_at": 1790381063.571397, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "4f89de37-f85f-4855-81f8-f0743d9c17f7", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790381063.573917, "updated_at": 1790381063.573917, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "b881afb3-d0e7-48fe-885e-981ecb334266", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790381063.575473, "updated_at": 1790383142.310759, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yes. **This is V3.** I’d treat it as the first complete, coherent version of the session-frame contract rather than another incremental tweak.\n\nThe design is now cleanly separated into **human orientation**, **Don intent**, **context management**, **session outcome**, and **machine routing**.\n\n# GCE SESSION HEADER / FOOTER — V3\n\n## 1. Core Session Header\n\nThis is the **always-visible orientation block**. It should stay compact.\n\n```text\n==================================================\nGCE SESSION HEADER — V3\n==================================================\n\nTIMESTAMP:            <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM TZ>\n\nAUTHORITY:            Don\nPRIMARY SEAT:         <seat>\nOCCUPANT / MODEL:     <model/provider/runtime>\n\nMODE:                 <RECONCILIATION | IMPLEMENTATION |\n                       VERIFICATION | ARCHITECTURE |\n                       ADVISORY | RESEARCH | OPERATIONS>\n\nCURRENT THREAD:       <short stable thread/workstream name>\n\nCURRENT CONTEXT:      <1–2 lines describing exactly where we are\n                       inside the current thread>\n\nPRIORITY:             <HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW>\n\nMATURITY:             <POC | DEVELOPMENT | VALIDATION |\n                       PRODUCTION-READY | PRODUCTION>\n\nSTATUS:               <ACTIVE | CHECKPOINT | BLOCKED |\n                       PARKED | COMPLETE>\n\nCONFIDENCE:           <0–100%>\n\nSTARTED:              <original thread/workstream timestamp>\nDAYS RUNNING:         <calculated automatically>\nACTIVE DAYS:          <calculated automatically>\nLAST ACTIVE:          <latest recorded activity timestamp>\n\nCURRENT ANCHOR:       <current authoritative artifact/ruling/state pointer>\n```\n\n---\n\n# 2. Header Appendix A — Don Intent Snapshot\n\nThis is the **voice-to-framework interpretation check**.\n\nIt is deliberately short.\n\n```text\n--------------------------------------------------\nHEADER APPENDIX A — DON INTENT SNAPSHOT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nRAW INTENT:\n<1–2 lines capturing what Don is actually saying/requesting>\n\nOBJECTIVE:\n<the concrete outcome Don is trying to achieve>\n\nCONTEXT:\n<why this matters / surrounding constraint / relevant state>\n```\n\n### Rule\n\nThis appendix is **interpretive, not authoritative**.\n\nIf Don says:\n\n> No, that's not what I meant.\n\nthen this block gets corrected immediately.\n\nIt exists specifically so interpretation errors become visible **before execution**.\n\n---\n\n# 3. Header Appendix B — Active Context Board\n\nThis solves the context-switching problem.\n\n```text\n--------------------------------------------------\nHEADER APPENDIX B — ACTIVE CONTEXT BOARD\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nPROMOTED / CURRENT:\n- <the one thing currently being worked>\n\nPARKED:\n- <thread/workstream>\n  State: <short state>\n\n- <thread/workstream>\n  State: <short state>\n\n- <thread/workstream>\n  State: <short state>\n```\n\n### Promotion rule\n\nOnly **one item is promoted/current**.\n\nWhen Don switches:\n\n```text\nOLD CURRENT → PARKED\nNEW ITEM    → PROMOTED\n```\n\nWe do **not** silently change lanes.\n\nAnd promotion does **not** reset:\n\n- `STARTED`\n- `DAYS RUNNING`\n- `ACTIVE DAYS`\n\nThose describe the overall session/thread lifecycle.\n\n---\n\n# 4. Lifecycle / KPI Semantics\n\nThese should be deterministic.\n\n```text\nSTARTED\n= when the overall thread/workstream began\n\nDAYS RUNNING\n= calendar days from STARTED through today, inclusive\n\nACTIVE DAYS\n= distinct calendar days with recorded activity\n\nLAST ACTIVE\n= most recent recorded activity timestamp\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nSTARTED:        2026-09-23 15:59 PT\nDAYS RUNNING:   3\nACTIVE DAYS:    2\nLAST ACTIVE:    2026-09-25 16:56 PT\n```\n\nThis becomes the foundation for future Framework KPIs.\n\nLater we can derive things like:\n\n```text\nHANDOFFS\nSEAT TRANSITIONS\nGATES PASSED\nBLOCKERS\nREWORK LOOPS\nAVERAGE CONFIDENCE\nTIME BLOCKED\nHIGH-PRIORITY AGING\n```\n\nThose do **not** belong in the core header yet.\n\n---\n\n# 5. Core Session Footer\n\nThe footer stays deliberately lean.\n\nIt answers:\n\n**What happened? How sure are we? What's unresolved? Where does this go next?**\n\n```text\n==================================================\nGCE SESSION FOOTER — V3\n==================================================\n\nSEAT:                 <current seat>\nSESSION STATUS:       <CHECKPOINT | BLOCKED |\n                       PARKED | COMPLETE>\n\nOUTCOME:\n<1–3 lines describing what materially happened>\n\nCONFIDENCE:           <0–100%>\n\nDECISIONS:\n- <accepted decision>\n- <accepted decision>\n\nBLOCKERS:\n- <real blocker only>\n\nOPEN ITEMS:\n- <unfinished item>\n\nNEXT ROUTE:           <seat / Don / NONE>\n\nNEXT ACTION:\n<one precise continuation action>\n\nHANDOFF:              <handoff ID/path or NONE>\n```\n\nNo Cable Car telemetry.\n\nNo full project-state dump.\n\nNo carousel state.\n\nNo five-paragraph routing explanation.\n\nThose go below.\n\n---\n\n# 6. Footer Appendix A — Routing / Handoff Packet\n\nThis is the **machine-facing continuation contract**.\n\n```text\n--------------------------------------------------\nFOOTER APPENDIX A — ROUTING / HANDOFF\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nPROJECT:              <project identifier>\nWORKSTREAM:           <workstream identifier>\n\nSESSION_ID:           <stable session ID>\n\nCURRENT_SEAT:         <seat>\nNEXT_ROUTE:           <seat / Don / NONE>\nAFTER_PASS:           <optional seat>\nFINAL_GATE:           <optional seat / Don>\n\nGATE:                 <current gate>\nBLOCKER_ROUTE:        <seat / Don / NONE>\n\nCURRENT_ANCHOR:       <artifact/state pointer>\n\nHANDOFF_ID:           <stable handoff ID>\nHANDOFF_TYPE:         <type>\n\nLOCAL_HANDOFF_PATH:\n<absolute local path>\n\nDRIVE_HANDOFF_URL:\n<Google Drive URL if published>\n\nDRIVE_ARTIFACT_ID:\n<Drive artifact ID if available>\n\nCABLE_CAR_STATE:\n<NONE | QUEUED | PUBLISHED | RECEIVED | ERROR>\n```\n\nThis is where Cable Car belongs.\n\nNot in the human footer.\n\n---\n\n# 7. Local + Drive Handoff Model\n\nOne handoff should have **one identity** and multiple representations.\n\n```text\nHANDOFF_ID\n    │\n    ├── LOCAL_PATH\n    │\n    ├── DRIVE_ARTIFACT_ID\n    │\n    └── DRIVE_URL\n```\n\nNot:\n\n```text\nlocal handoff\n+\nsome unrelated Drive handoff\n```\n\nThe artifact is the artifact.\n\nCable Car transports/publishes it.\n\nThat gives us the experience we want later:\n\n```text\n[ OPEN LOCAL ]     [ OPEN DRIVE ]\n```\n\nOpenCode can act on the local path.\n\nYou and I can inspect the persistent Drive copy.\n\nSame `HANDOFF_ID`.\n\n---\n\n# 8. Priority Contract\n\nKeep this intentionally simple:\n\n```text\nHIGH\nMEDIUM\nLOW\n```\n\n### HIGH\n\nPrimary build, blocking work, production-impacting work, or something Don is actively driving.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nMain DevPad\n```\n\n### MEDIUM\n\nImportant enabling work that should move, but does not displace the primary build.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nSession Controller / Carousel\n```\n\n### LOW\n\nUseful improvement that can safely wait.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nVoiceBridge tweaks\n```\n\nNo priority inflation.\n\nNo P0/P1/P2 layer on top of it.\n\n---\n\n# 9. Maturity Is Different From Status\n\nThis distinction should stay explicit.\n\n### Maturity\n\n```text\nPOC\nDEVELOPMENT\nVALIDATION\nPRODUCTION-READY\nPRODUCTION\n```\n\nThis answers:\n\n> How mature is the thing?\n\n### Status\n\n```text\nACTIVE\nCHECKPOINT\nBLOCKED\nPARKED\nCOMPLETE\n```\n\nThis answers:\n\n> What is happening with it right now?\n\nSo something can legitimately be:\n\n```text\nMATURITY: DEVELOPMENT\nSTATUS:   PARKED\nPRIORITY: LOW\n```\n\nor:\n\n```text\nMATURITY: PRODUCTION\nSTATUS:   BLOCKED\nPRIORITY: HIGH\n```\n\nThose dimensions should never be collapsed.\n\n---\n\n# 10. Full V3 Example\n\n```text\n==================================================\nGCE SESSION HEADER — V3\n==================================================\n\nTIMESTAMP:            2026-09-25 16:56 PT\n\nAUTHORITY:            Don\nPRIMARY SEAT:         Coda\nOCCUPANT / MODEL:     GPT-5.6 Sol\n\nMODE:                 RECONCILIATION\nCURRENT THREAD:       Framework Taxonomy / Routing Reconciliation\n\nCURRENT CONTEXT:      Reconcile current machine truth against the\n                      accepted Framework before Nico implementation.\n\nPRIORITY:             HIGH\nMATURITY:             DEVELOPMENT\nSTATUS:               ACTIVE\nCONFIDENCE:           97%\n\nSTARTED:              2026-09-23 15:59 PT\nDAYS RUNNING:         3\nACTIVE DAYS:          3\nLAST ACTIVE:          2026-09-25 16:56 PT\n\nCURRENT ANCHOR:       Luce current-state reconciliation\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nHEADER APPENDIX A — DON INTENT SNAPSHOT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nRAW INTENT:\nDon wants the actual Framework machine state reconciled before\nmore controller or routing automation is layered on top.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\nProduce one trustworthy correction package that Nico can implement\nwithout another discovery/reconciliation loop.\n\nCONTEXT:\nSeat/bootstrap switching already works. Remaining friction is largely\ncanon, routing, storage and control-plane inconsistency.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nHEADER APPENDIX B — ACTIVE CONTEXT BOARD\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nPROMOTED / CURRENT:\n- Framework Taxonomy / Routing Reconciliation\n\nPARKED:\n\n- Main DevPad\n  State: active development\n\n- Session Controller / Carousel\n  State: accepted direction; implementation deferred\n\n- Cable Car / Google Drive\n  State: functional transport; contract/taxonomy work pending\n\n- Open Handoff\n  State: Nico utility spec prepared\n\n- Mobile Orchestration / Vomit Runtime\n  State: architectural concept\n\n\n==================================================\nSESSION WORK\n==================================================\n\n\n==================================================\nGCE SESSION FOOTER — V3\n==================================================\n\nSEAT:                 Coda\nSESSION STATUS:       CHECKPOINT\n\nOUTCOME:\nCurrent Framework state reconciled and bounded correction package\nprepared for implementation.\n\nCONFIDENCE:           97%\n\nDECISIONS:\n- Project owns project-specific implementation truth.\n- Routing destination does not determine artifact ownership.\n- Model occupant does not define seat identity.\n\nBLOCKERS:\n- <none or actual blocker>\n\nOPEN ITEMS:\n- <remaining unresolved item>\n\nNEXT ROUTE:           Nico\n\nNEXT ACTION:\nExecute accepted Framework correction package.\n\nHANDOFF:              GCE-HO-20260925-0042\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nFOOTER APPENDIX A — ROUTING / HANDOFF\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nPROJECT:              GCE_Framework\nWORKSTREAM:           Taxonomy_Reconciliation\nSESSION_ID:           20260925-CODA-001\n\nCURRENT_SEAT:         Coda\nNEXT_ROUTE:           Nico\nAFTER_PASS:           Luce\nFINAL_GATE:           Don\n\nGATE:                 IMPLEMENTATION\nBLOCKER_ROUTE:        Don/Coda\n\nCURRENT_ANCHOR:       <anchor>\n\nHANDOFF_ID:           GCE-HO-20260925-0042\nHANDOFF_TYPE:         governance_to_implementation\n\nLOCAL_HANDOFF_PATH:\nC:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\...\\20260925-CODA-TO-NICO.md\n\nDRIVE_HANDOFF_URL:\n<Drive URL>\n\nDRIVE_ARTIFACT_ID:\n<Drive ID>\n\nCABLE_CAR_STATE:      PUBLISHED\n```\n\n## V3 design doctrine\n\nThe clean summary is:\n\n> **Header = where we are.**  \n> **Intent Snapshot = what Don means.**  \n> **Context Board = what is current versus parked.**  \n> **Footer = what happened and what happens next.**  \n> **Routing Appendix = how the machines continue it.**\n\nAnd the lifecycle/KPI fields mean we're no longer just recording state—we're starting to measure **how the Framework operates over time**.\n\nI would use **`GCE_SESSION_FRAME_V3`** as the anchor name when we drop the anchor next.", "text_chars": 11456, "code_blocks": 21, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": ["Brother\\...\\20260925-CODA-TO-NICO.md", "C:\\Users\\Dekan"], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "b472f05e-d2c0-42c8-a13d-569a1ec8e33f", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790381122.224083, "updated_at": 1790381138.77279, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Okay, this is the main session header and footer whenever we start each day, right? Whenever I pick up a conversation and it's a new day, it's the new session header and footer. It's almost our automated anchor.", "text_chars": 211, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "ac74c459-18f5-422f-9f35-6556e0b3bbe2", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790381124.989472, "updated_at": 1790384111.191392, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Exactly. **That’s the right role for V3.**\n\nIt becomes the **daily session anchor** for any continuing conversation/workstream.\n\nAt the start of a new day, we generate a fresh header/footer frame that says, in effect:\n\n> **Here is where this thread stands today.**\n\nThe thread itself persists, but the **daily session frame resets**.\n\nSo the model is:\n\n```text\nLONG-RUNNING THREAD / WORKSTREAM\n        │\n        ├── Day 1 Session Header/Footer\n        ├── Day 2 Session Header/Footer\n        ├── Day 3 Session Header/Footer\n        └── Day N Session Header/Footer\n```\n\nAnd each new-day header should automatically carry forward only the durable state:\n\n- authority\n- current thread\n- current anchor\n- priority\n- maturity\n- start date\n- days running\n- active days\n- parked workstreams\n- unresolved blockers\n- latest accepted decisions\n- last route/handoff\n\nThen it refreshes the session-specific fields:\n\n- **TIMESTAMP**\n- **MODE**\n- **CURRENT CONTEXT**\n- **STATUS**\n- **CONFIDENCE**\n- **LAST ACTIVE**\n- **Don Intent Snapshot**\n- **promoted/current work item**\n\nSo yes: it is basically an **automated daily re-anchor**.\n\nAnd I would make one rule explicit:\n\n> **A new day creates a new session frame, not a new thread.**\n\nThat means `STARTED` stays the original workstream start date and `DAYS RUNNING` keeps increasing, while the daily session gets a new `SESSION_ID`.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nTHREAD: Framework Taxonomy / Routing Reconciliation\nSTARTED: 2026-09-23\nDAYS RUNNING: 4\n\nSESSION_ID: 20260926-CODA-001\nTIMESTAMP: 2026-09-26 09:14 PT\n```\n\nThe footer from the previous day becomes the **input anchor** for the next day's header.\n\nSo the daily cycle is:\n\n```text\nYESTERDAY FOOTER\n      ↓\nlatest accepted anchor / handoff / decisions\n      ↓\nNEW DAY HEADER\n      ↓\ntoday's work\n      ↓\nTODAY FOOTER\n```\n\nThat gives us the continuity we’ve been missing without relying on the model to reconstruct everything from conversation history.\n\nI’d freeze this rule into V3 as:\n\n> **SESSION FRAME ROLLOVER:** On the first interaction with a continuing thread on a new calendar day, create a new V3 Session Header using the prior session footer plus the current authoritative anchor. Preserve thread lifecycle metrics; reset only daily session state.\n\nThat turns V3 into exactly what you called it: **our automated anchor.**", "text_chars": 2314, "code_blocks": 3, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "f8bb9237-d6b3-46e1-81e1-ef3b87aef4c5", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790381153.515983, "updated_at": 1790381278.251961, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Perfect. And then what we're gonna do now, go through Google Drive, look at the current framework, session header and footer, and see what's designed, and make sure this is now canonical moving forward.", "text_chars": 202, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "9b8a400b-a5e1-402d-a7ee-7e257fc1842d", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790381158.258134, "updated_at": 1790381159.087569, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "functions.exec", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "286bd1bc-ec1c-4771-943d-e91a7aa73b95", "role": "tool", "role_name": "functions.exec", "created_at": 1790381159.351641, "updated_at": 1790381159.351641, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "a6b67566-fe13-412a-924b-c63b031845c7", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790381160.990586, "updated_at": 1790381161.619568, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "functions.exec", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "0e7295bd-9591-4262-9dfc-32f9d5c676f3", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790381162.305323, "updated_at": 1790381162.305323, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "api_tool.call_tool", "content_type": "code", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations":