"model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "67416713-d83b-4d19-819f-0714d7a9e368", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790382261.049125, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "c847fa27-98e9-46ec-97a7-b41568676a01", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790382261.049678, "updated_at": 1790382262.737019, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Alright, so, what I’d do is codify a single bootstrap contract that both terminal and chat obey. So, same contract, different surface. The identity never changes with the model. On bootstrap, we must load in order: current Don authority, current Framework canon, current seat/roster doctrine, current daily session anchor, then to-do list, then runtime capabilities. Mid-flight and checkpoint are subordinate controls under that anchor. And no silent lane changes. No model == seat drift. And confidence is never optional. So, the artifacts I put in place are Coda bootstrap V1, tied to Session Frame V3 and the subordinate Mid-Flight and Checkpoint controls. And we can refine it as we see the actual terminal bootstrap.", "text_chars": 722, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "3d729929-26dc-49af-b959-e0f50b04a7f7", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790382261.6386092, "updated_at": 1790382326.8708, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Yes, the only thing you have to add to it And I think I'm fixing it right now is the cable car process for inbound and outbound for you", "text_chars": 136, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "b2aeb619-342e-4023-b735-aff438fe629f", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790382325.285554, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Let me check that.", "text_chars": 19, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "a654a6c3-1af3-4697-b7d0-8a0dd9654547", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790382325.286679, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "9f0cab43-8229-4345-8aee-cac9c3de75c8", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790382325.287277, "updated_at": 1790382326.871021, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Let me check that. Yep, that’s the missing piece. We make the cable car behavior explicit inside the bootstrap. So, define inbound intake and outbound handoff as part of startup, not tribal knowledge. Inbound means what channels Coda listens to, how they're named, where they land, how they are validated and how they get reconciled into the current context, and outbound means when Coda emits a handoff, what structure it must have, where it gets stored, how it's labeled, and how transport state is recorded without confusing it with session state. That keeps parity with terminal and makes cable car a first-class part of how Coda wakes up. Inbound to me, outbound from me, and neither changes ownership or authority. Just moves the package.", "text_chars": 745, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "150e5797-4943-4eb0-86ba-385d9fdab6f1", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790382339.926775, "updated_at": 1790382473.993418, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Perfect, review your bootstrap, create it in... Jesus, create it in Google Drive, etc. Do the recon, set it up yourself. You got this.", "text_chars": 134, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "07248089-a438-4022-9ed4-849c1ca27831", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790382342.167799, "updated_at": 1790382342.167799, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "model_editable_context", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "2e536574-12c4-4592-b7e1-4d1e272bee60", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790382343.635091, "updated_at": 1790382346.393395, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "functions.exec", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references