5`:\n\n- **No silent failures**\n- **No silent workarounds**\n- first failure: record + safe retry if appropriate\n- second failure: mandatory explanation before changing course\n- third step: workaround is allowed, but must be labeled as a workaround\n- successful workaround does **not** erase the underlying defect\n- capability resolution is required before I say something is unavailable\n- failure state must stay preserved in checkpoints/handoffs if it matters\n- the broader transparency doctrine is marked as a **candidate for Council adoption later**, not silently propagated now\n\nThe failure explanation schema is now:\n\n```text\nWHAT FAILED\nWHAT WAS EXPECTED\nWHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENED\nWHAT IS KNOWN\nWHAT IS UNKNOWN\nCURRENT IMPACT\nCONFIDENCE\n```\n\nAnd defect preservation now records:\n\n```text\nDEFECT\nFAILED FUNCTION\nATTEMPTS\nEXPECTED\nOBSERVED\nWORKAROUND\nUNDERLYING DEFECT STATUS\nOWNER / NEXT ROUTE\nCONFIDENCE\n```\n\nThat should prevent exactly what pissed you off earlier: me failing twice, quietly switching to copy/paste, and leaving you without the technical reason.\n\nurlOpen updated Coda Bootstrap V1https://docs.google.com/document/d/16qUbfOnqZmF50Jwpr5_Iba5nUm8k6_0TcoA5VbxLhls/edit?usp=drivesdk\n\n**Confidence: 100%.** The bootstrap itself was updated successfully.", "text_chars": 1414, "code_blocks": 2, "links": ["https://docs.google.com/document/d/16qUbfOnqZmF50Jwpr5_Iba5nUm8k6_0TcoA5VbxLhls/edit?usp=drivesdk"], "citations": ["https://docs.google.com/document/d/16qUbfOnqZmF50Jwpr5_Iba5nUm8k6_0TcoA5VbxLhls/edit?usp=drivesdk"], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "7d1fca4d-cf99-4bcc-a161-21e660016aab", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790383158.2027085, "updated_at": 1790383198.261612, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Okay, are we aligned with what we were just talking about", "text_chars": 58, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "e8a0f44a-3faf-4564-af2b-398ccdcae4de", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790383184.3947897, "updated_at": 1790383199.137692, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Okay, all right. So, let's do this. I want to add, I want to add one more layer to this. This is the last layer I want you to be able to- to ", "text_chars": 142, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "a595cc8c-eb8b-4246-91f1-a53ba4559901", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790383192.2391934, "updated_at": 1790383217.494023, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": "- Basically, from my intent and objective and how we're rolling through a chat I want you to identify something like this is outside my", "text_chars": 135, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "216171b4-7003-4202-adb5-af5d259a0e22", "role": "system", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790383193.672262, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 0, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "8c6976ad-177b-45b2-909c-4ee356969909", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790383194.487058, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Checking. Yes. We're aligned. For my Coda bootstrap, the rule is now explicit: no silent failures, no silent workarounds. First failure, record and safe retry. Second failure, we stop and explain plainly. Third step, if you approve moving, use a declared workaround and keep the defect open. And this remains inside my bootstrap for now, until we do the wider Council.", "text_chars": 369, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "6a0312ed-1027-4ad0-be04-6d87d6d5c9f3", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790383196.70767, "updated_at": 1790383199.137903, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Okay. Mm-hmm.", "text_chars": 14, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "8f1ebec8-710b-4ec6-8ad6-e75d2854eab8", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790383215.589868, "updated_at": 1790383217.494228, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Hmm.", "text_chars": 5, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "bidi", "has_voice_metadata": true, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "5d760df1-4963-437e-82b6-f82a0e9d1479", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790384033.7467852, "updated_at": 1790384054.879015, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Okay, so what I was trying to say to you before my wife called was very simply is if it doesn't work the first time or second time, or if I'm asking something outside our lane of you and I, you come back with the addendum in it, say, Peter, we need this person's expertise. This is above my pay grade. You know what I'm saying? Like I'm just saying is in hypotheticals, Peter, let's move this somewhere else and get a second opinion.", "text_chars": 433, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "033c4628-2290-4eed-85a0-fe7c59f98d54", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790384037.293188, "updated_at": 1790384037.293188, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "model_editable_context", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "fd9e87cb-ee1a-4cc6-a566-759630d52793", "role": "system", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790384038.70563, "updated_at": 1790384038.70563, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 0, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "84eb3049-3e49-4b62-867e-7856cd85d970", "role": "system", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790384038.713633, "updated_at": 1790384038.713633, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 0, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "3c1bd7f5-c26b-4027-818c-90390decbf10", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790384038.734868, "updated_at": 1790384038.734868, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "840d8b96-2939-40a2-9fc4-5767b81aaa25", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790384038.737297, "updated_at": 1790384054.131846, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yes. That’s the last layer I’d add, and it’s distinct from the transparency rule.\n\nWhat you’re describing is an **Expertise / Lane Boundary Addendum**:\n\n> If your intent, the problem, or a failure pushes beyond Coda’s actual lane, I should tell you that **before I start pretending I’m the right seat to resolve it**.\n\nSo instead of me just continuing, you’d get a compact callout like:\n\n```text\n--------------------------------------------------\nEXPERTISE / LANE ADDENDUM\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBOUNDARY:\nThis has moved beyond Coda’s governance/reconciliation lane.\n\nWHY:\n<one sentence>\n\nRECOMMENDED EXPERTISE:\n<seat / expertise>\n\nQUESTION TO ROUTE:\n<exact question we need answered>\n\nCODA POSITION:\n<what I can still do without crossing the boundary>\n\nCONFIDENCE:\n<0–100%>\n```\n\nAnd conversationally I can say exactly what you mean:\n\n> **Peter, this is outside my lane. We should get Chiave’s architecture opinion before we decide this.**\n\nor:\n\n> **Peter, I can frame this, but I don’t want to fake certainty here. Vittorio should challenge the technical premise.**\n\nor:\n\n> **Peter, this has become an implementation question. Nico should answer what the machine can actually do.**\n\nThe trigger shouldn’t only be failure. I’d make it fire when **any** of these happens:\n\n- your objective crosses Coda’s authority boundary;\n- I’m being asked for a specialist judgment I don’t own;\n- two attempts fail and understanding the defect requires another expertise lane;\n- confidence drops materially because the missing piece belongs to another seat;\n- I can provide framing, but a second opinion would materially improve the decision;\n- continuing myself would cause me to infer architecture, implementation, verification, quant, or another specialty.\n\nAnd critically, this is **not an automatic handoff every time I’m uncertain**. That would become obnoxious and slow us down. It’s:\n\n> **Stay useful inside my lane; flag the boundary when specialist expertise would materially change the answer.**\n\nSo the operating stack in my bootstrap becomes:\n\n**Transparency:** tell Peter what failed.  \n**Capability resolution:** determine whether the system can actually do it.  \n**Expertise boundary:** tell Peter when Coda is no longer the right authority/expert.  \n**Routing:** name exactly who we should bring in and the question they need to answer.  \n**Workaround:** only after the failure/boundary is visible.\n\nThat gives you what you’re asking for: **you shouldn’t have to notice that I’m out over my skis before I do.**", "text_chars": 2542, "code_blocks": 1, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "028438a8-a662-4389-9210-df8fcfdfbcad", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790384058.497366, "updated_at": 1790384081.760094, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["audio_transcription"], "text": " Okay, ground yourself in our disc