s. Same style — short, Italian-rooted, function over flash. Here's the full roster:\n\n**Coda** — *you let him name his own intern, so I leave that seat open for him.*\n\n**Chiave** (Independent Architecture Seat / Architecture Gate) — **Muro**. The wall. Chiave holds the gate; Muro is the wall that says \"nothing passes that isn't structurally sound.\" Not a challenger like Vittorio — a *barrier*. The architecture doesn't get to vote; it gets to *stop*.\n\n**Corrado** (Quant Engine) — **Abaco**. The abacus. Corrado is pure math, pure calculation — Abaco is the oldest computing machine, relentless, mechanical, *true*. No narrative, no story — just the number.\n\n**Falcon** (Data Acquisition / Retrieval) — **Falco**. The hawk. Falcon already carries the bird; Falco sharpens it. He sees the data from altitude, dives fast, and comes back with exactly what was asked. No interpretation — just the catch.\n\n**Talon** (Operations / Routing / Coordination) — **Volo**. The flight. Talon routes the puck; Volo is the movement itself — the pass that connects the defense to the offense without anyone noticing. The seam.\n\n**Keel** (Deployment / Operational Build Support / Stability) — **Chiglia**. The keel of the ship. Below the waterline, invisible, but the whole vessel rests on it. Keel doesn't get credit; Keel keeps the ship upright.\n\n**Luce** (Verification / Ground Truth) — **Specchio**. The mirror. Luce is already light; Specchio is what the light hits. It reflects exactly what is — no distortion, no flattery. The ground truth stares back.\n\n**Magpie** (Registry / Secretary) — **Archivio**. The archive. Magpie collects; Archivio *keeps*. Every decision, every hash, every version — recorded, filed, retrievable. The memory of the organization.\n\n**Pigeon** (Transport) — **Rondine**. The swallow. Pigeon carries; Rondine is the migratory bird that *always finds the way home*. Messages, artifacts, handoffs — delivered, no matter the distance.\n\n**Raven** (Documentation) — **Calamaio**. The inkwell. Raven documents; Calamaio is the ink that makes it permanent. Not the quill — the *ink*. The substance that makes the record indelible.\n\n---\n\n**The full team, Don:**\n\n| Seat | Name | Function |\n|------|------|----------|\n| Coda | *(his choice)* | Strategic Advisor / Governance |\n| Vittorio | **Sable** | Technical Advisor / Warboard / Challenge |\n| Chiave | **Muro** | Architecture Gate |\n| Nico | **Ferro** | Implementation Hammer |\n| Corrado | **Abaco** | Quant Engine |\n| Falcon | **Falco** | Data Acquisition |\n| Talon | **Volo** | Operations / Routing |\n| Keel | **Chiglia** | Deployment / Stability |\n| Luce | **Specchio** | Verification / Ground Truth |\n| Magpie | **Archivio** | Registry / Secretary |\n| Pigeon | **Rondine** | Transport |\n| Raven | **Calamaio** | Documentation |\n\nTwelve seats, twelve functions, one Don above them all.\n\nWhere do you want to tweak?", "text_chars": 2894, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "7079af96-112d-490f-824d-aedd7e7c2310", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790392632.977702, "updated_at": 1790392641.338885, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yep — **this is a clean naming layer**. It fits the framework well because the names are memorable without pretending to be authority.\n\nA couple of precision points so we don’t contaminate the bootstrap doctrine:\n\n- **Seat identity stays the seat**: Chiave, Corrado, Falcon, Talon, etc.\n- **Muro / Abaco / Falco / Volo / Chiglia / Specchio / Archivio / Rondine / Calamaio** should be treated as the **made-person / symbolic identity layer**, not replacement seat names.\n- Same for **Sable** under Vittorio and **Ferro** under Nico.\n- They can help behavior/memory, but they do **not** redefine role, authority, routing, or ownership.\n\nSo the canonical shape becomes:\n\n| Seat | Made-person identity | Function |\n|---|---|---|\n| Coda | *(self-selected later)* | Strategic Advisor / Governance |\n| Vittorio | **Sable** | Technical Advisor / Warboard / Challenge |\n| Chiave | **Muro** | Architecture Gate |\n| Nico | **Ferro** | Implementation Hammer |\n| Corrado | **Abaco** | Quant Engine |\n| Falcon | **Falco** | Data Acquisition |\n| Talon | **Volo** | Operations / Routing |\n| Keel | **Chiglia** | Deployment / Stability |\n| Luce | **Specchio** | Verification / Ground Truth |\n| Magpie | **Archivio** | Registry / Secretary |\n| Pigeon | **Rondine** | Transport |\n| Raven | **Calamaio** | Documentation |\n\n**Coda remains open by design** until Coda self-selects that layer.\n\nThe only thing I’d flag for later bootstrap integration is this: we should add these as **identity metadata**, not as the primary labels in routing or registry keys. That keeps `MODEL != SEAT` and `IDENTITY != ROLE != AUTHORITY` intact.", "text_chars": 1608, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "204be713-b253-4a23-ac7f-f2caf6e689a4", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790392657.0611959, "updated_at": 1790392668.584595, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "You are Coda, buddy. You get to name your intern on the rookie guy.", "text_chars": 67, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "a07928b2-3b74-4bbe-bde3-454f34787f2c", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790392658.996857, "updated_at": 1790392658.996857, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "model_editable_cont