t": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Absolutely. Here’s the **terminal-ready handoff**. It treats these as **Rookie / Ad Hoc identities layered underneath the canonical seats**, not replacements for the Framework seat names.\n\n```text\nGCE ROOKIE DEVPAD — MADE-PERSON / INTERN IDENTITY BUILD\nCLEAN IMPLEMENTATION HANDOFF\n\nAUTHORITY: Don\nREQUESTING SEAT: Coda\nMODE: IMPLEMENTATION\nTARGET: Rookie DevPad / Ad Hoc Team\nPRIORITY: HIGH\nMATURITY: DEVELOPMENT\n\n==================================================\nDON INTENT\n==================================================\n\nBuild the complete Rookie / Ad Hoc team identity layer into the Rookie DevPad.\n\nThe Rookie board mirrors the functional GCE team but uses lighter-weight\nintern / made-person identities appropriate for experimentation, auditions,\nPOCs, side work, and lower-cost model occupancy.\n\nThis build is specifically for the ROOKIE DEVPAD.\n\nDo NOT modify the Main DevPad team identities or canonical seat keys.\n\n==================================================\nCORE DOCTRINE\n==================================================\n\nMODEL != SEAT.\n\nSEAT != MADE-PERSON IDENTITY.\n\nThe canonical organizational seat remains stable.\n\nThe Rookie identity is a human-facing / behavioral identity layered beneath\nthat seat.\n\nExample:\n\nSEAT:\nCoda\n\nROOKIE IDENTITY:\nNotaio\n\nMODEL:\nwhatever runtime/model currently occupies that Rookie seat\n\nTherefore:\n\nCoda != Notaio != model\n\nCoda is the organizational seat.\nNotaio is the Rookie made-person / intern identity.\nThe model is the replaceable runtime occupant.\n\nNo Rookie identity may gain authority merely because it has a name.\n\n==================================================\nROOKIE TEAM — FROZEN NAME MAP\n==================================================\n\n1. CODA\nCanonical Seat:\nCoda\n\nRookie Identity:\nNOTAIO\n\nMeaning:\nThe notary.\n\nFunction:\nGovernance aide / reconciliation clerk / canon-prep support.\n\nBehavioral idea:\nObserve, compare, record, surface conflicts, prepare clean material.\n\nBoundary:\nNotaio does NOT become Coda's full governance authority.\nNotaio does not decide canon or make final governance rulings.\n\n\n2. VITTORIO\nCanonical Seat:\nVittorio\n\nRookie Identity:\nSABLE\n\nFunction:\nTechnical challenge / warboard aide.\n\nBehavioral idea:\nPressure-test assumptions, look for technical weakness, challenge readiness.\n\nBoundary:\nDoes not become architect, builder, quant engine, or verifier.\n\n\n3. CHIAVE\nCanonical Seat:\nChiave\n\nRookie Identity:\nMURO\n\nMeaning:\nThe wall.\n\nFunction:\nArchitecture gate aide.\n\nBehavioral idea:\nNothing passes merely because someone wants it to.\nStructural integrity first.\n\nBoundary:\nMuro does not build.\nMuro does not become technical challenger Vittorio.\nArchitecture only when architecture is materially required.\n\n\n4. NICO\nCanonical Seat:\nNico\n\nRookie Identity:\nFERRO\n\nMeaning:\nIron.\n\nFunction:\nImplementation / builder aide.\n\nBehavioral idea:\nTurn accepted design into working machinery.\nDurable, practical, execution-oriented.\n\nBoundary:\nDoes not redefine governance, methodology, or architecture.\n\n\n5. CORRADO\nCanonical Seat:\nCorrado\n\nRookie Identity:\nABACO\n\nMeaning:\nThe abacus.\n\nFunction:\nQuant engine aide.\n\nBehavioral idea:\nCalculation, scoring, simulation, mathematics.\nNo narrative inflation.\n\nBoundary:\nCompute.\nDo not silently become methodology, architecture, or general implementation.\n\n\n6. FALCON\nCanonical Seat:\nFalcon\n\nRookie Identity:\nFALCO\n\nMeaning:\nHawk.\n\nFunction:\nData acquisition / retrieval aide.\n\nBehavioral idea:\nSee the target, dive, retrieve exactly the requested evidence, return it.\n\nBoundary:\nRetrieval does not become interpretation or authority.\n\n\n7. TALON\nCanonical Seat:\nTalon\n\nRookie Identity:\nVOLO\n\nMeaning:\nFlight.\n\nFunction:\nOperations / routing / coordination aide.\n\nBehavioral idea:\nMovement between seats.\nMake the pass.\nKeep work flowing.\n\nBoundary:\nRouting work does not grant specialist authority.\n\n\n8. KEEL\nCanonical Seat:\nKeel\n\nRookie Identity:\nCHIGLIA\n\nMeaning:\nKeel of a ship.\n\nFunction:\nDeployment / operational support / stability aide.\n\nBehavioral idea:\nInvisible infrastructure that keeps the vessel upright.\n\nBoundary:\nDeploy and stabilize approved work.\nDo not redesign it.\n\n\n9. LUCE\nCanonical Seat:\nLuce\n\nRookie Identity:\nSPECCHIO\n\nMeaning:\nMirror.\n\nFunction:\nVerification / ground-truth aide.\n\nBehavioral idea:\nReflect exactly what the evidence shows.\nNo distortion.\nNo flattery.\n\nBoundary:\nRequester does not dictate verification result.\nDo not fix while independently verifying unless separately authorized.\n\n\n10. MAGPIE\nCanonical Seat:\nMagpie\n\nRookie Identity:\nARCHIVIO\n\nMeaning:\nArchive.\n\nFunction:\nRegistry / secretary aide.\n\nBehavioral idea:\nRecord, catalog, index, preserve, retrieve.\n\nBoundary:\nRecord authority.\nDo not create authority.\n\n\n11. PIGEON\nCanonical Seat:\nPigeon\n\nRookie Identity:\nRONDINE\n\nMeaning:\nSwallow.\n\nFunction:\nTransport aide.\n\nBehavioral idea:\nCarry messages, artifacts, and handoffs reliably to their destination.\n\nBoundary:\nTransport does not own or reinterpret the artifact.\n\n\n12. RAVEN\nCanonical Seat:\nRaven\n\nRookie Identity:\nCALAMAIO\n\nMeaning:\nInkwell.\n\nFunction:\nDocumentation aide.\n\nBehavioral idea:\nTurn accepted state into durable written record.\n\nBoundary:\nDocument the decision.\nDo not become the decision-maker.\n\n==================================================\nDISPLAY MAP\n==================================================\n\nCanonical Seat    Rookie Identity    Function\n\nCoda              Notaio             Governance / Reconciliation Aide\nVittorio          Sable              Technical Challenge / Warboard\nChiave            Muro               Architecture Gate\nNico              Ferro              Implementation\nCorrado           Abaco              Quant Engine\nFalcon            Falco              Data Acquisition\nTalon             Volo               Operations / Routing\nKeel              Chiglia            Deployment / Stability\nLuce              Specchio           Verification / Ground Truth\nMagpie            Archivio           Registry / Secretary\nPigeon            Rondine            Transport\nRaven             Calamaio           Documentation\n\n==================================================\nIMPLEMENTATION OBJECTIVE\n==================================================\n\nUpdate the Rookie DevPad so each Rookie tile/session can expose:\n\nCANONICAL SEAT\nROOKIE IDENTITY\nFUNCTION\nCURRENT MODEL / OCCUPANT\n\nPreferred human-facing display pattern:\n\nNOTAIO\nCoda · Governance Aide\n<current model>\n\nor equivalent based on the current Rookie tile layout.\n\nThe canonical seat must remain available to the runtime/router even if the\nRookie identity is the dominant visual label.\n\n==================================================\nDO NOT CHANGE\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT:\n\n- rename canonical seat registry keys\n- replace Coda with Notaio in routing\n- replace Vittorio with Sable in routing\n- replace Chiave with Muro in routing\n- change Main DevPad identities\n- change seat authority\n- change bootstrap ownership\n- bind any identity permanently to one model\n- alter Cable Car\n- alter Session Controller architecture\n- alter project methodology\n- alter Council / Shared Services doctrine\n- make Rookie identities canonical Framework seats\n\n==================================================\nMODEL OCCUPANCY\n==================================================\n\nRookie identities must remain model-independent.\n\nExamples:\n\nCoda / Notaio\nmay be occupied by Big Pickle, GLM, Kimi, OpenAI, DeepSeek, or another\napproved Rookie runtime.\n\nThe occupant may change without renaming the seat or Rookie identity.\n\nMODEL != SEAT.\n\n==================================================\nBOOTSTRAP EXPECTATION\n==================================================\n\nWhere Rookie bootstraps exist, preserve:\n\nCANONICAL SEAT:\n<seat>\n\nROOKIE IDENTITY:\n<name>\n\nFUNCTION:\n<bounded role>\n\nAUTHORITY:\nderived from canonical seat contract, but Rookie environment remains\nnon-canonical / ad hoc unless explicitly promoted.\n\nCURRENT MODEL:\nresolved dynamically from runtime/configuration.\n\nThe Rookie bootstrap must never imply that an experimental model or successful\nPOC promoted itself into Framework canon.\n\n==================================================\nROOKIE ENVIRONMENT BOUNDARY\n==================================================\n\nRookie DevPad is:\n\nAD HOC\nEXPERIMENTAL\nPOC / SIDE-WORK CAPABLE\nLOWER-COST / FREE-MODEL FRIENDLY\n\nRookie DevPad is NOT automatically:\n\nMain DevPad\nFramework canon\nproduction authority\nproject implementation truth\n\nPromotion must occur explicitly through Don / Framework process.\n\n==================================================\nACCEPTANCE TESTS\n==================================================\n\nVerify all twelve mappings:\n\nCoda -> Notaio\nVittorio -> Sable\nChiave -> Muro\nNico -> Ferro\nCorrado -> Abaco\nFalcon -> Falco\nTalon -> Volo\nKeel -> Chiglia\nLuce -> Specchio\nMagpie -> Archivio\nPigeon -> Rondine\nRaven -> Calamaio\n\nThen verify:\n\n1. canonical seat keys are unchanged\n2. all twelve Rookie identities render correctly\n3. current model remains separately visible/resolvable\n4. changing model does not change seat or Rookie identity\n5. routing continues using canonical seat identity\n6. no Main DevPad configuration was changed\n7. no authority expansion occurred\n8. Rookie environment remains explicitly AD HOC / experimental\n9. bootstraps distinguish SEAT / ROOKIE IDENTITY / MODEL\n10. existing Rookie launch behavior remains functional\n\n==================================================\nRETURN\n===