tation truth\n- current session-control schemas\n- current Drive taxonomy\n- model bindings\n\nThis is cleanup, not redesign.\n\n==================================================\nDELETE POLICY\n==================================================\n\nPermanent deletion is the LAST option.\n\nPrefer:\n\nKEEP\nor\nARCHIVE\nor\nCLEAR TRANSPORT COPY\n\nPermanent deletion only when all are true:\n\n- duplicate is proven\n- authoritative copy exists\n- no unique provenance exists\n- no live references exist\n- no unresolved ownership exists\n- hash/content evidence supports deletion\n\nIf uncertain:\nARCHIVE.\n\n==================================================\nSTOP CONDITIONS\n==================================================\n\nSTOP / CHECKPOINT before destructive action if:\n\n- no authoritative counterpart can be proven\n- lifecycle state is ambiguous\n- artifact ownership is unclear\n- active/current status conflicts\n- Drive/local copies disagree materially\n- hash mismatch appears where equality was expected\n- current routing references the candidate artifact\n- archive destination cannot be proven\n- cleanup would alter architecture or canon\n- a current Bootstrap/Rookie artifact appears mixed into historical queues\n- Don ruling is required\n\nDo not invent a compromise.\n\n==================================================\nVERIFICATION PHASE\n==================================================\n\nAfter archive/clear actions:\n\nVerify:\n\n1. all active inboxes enumerated\n2. all active handoff queues enumerated\n3. no active/unconsumed artifact lost\n4. no current/canonical artifact moved incorrectly\n5. no Rookie draft artifact moved\n6. current bootstrap evidence preserved\n7. current verification evidence preserved\n8. completed historical handoffs archived\n9. consumed inbox copies cleared\n10. duplicate removals proven\n11. archive manifest complete\n12. archive destination readable\n13. active queues contain only live/unknown work\n14. Cable Car runtime