d/reconciliation.\n\nIf authenticated Drive retrieval itself fails, report the exact command, exact error, and Drive ID attempted, then STOP.\n```\n\nThe larger lesson here is obvious: **every Rookie/runtime bootstrap needs the Drive/Cable Car retrieval contract baked into startup**, because otherwise every new model rediscovers this same problem and dumps the decision back on you.\n\nThat should go straight onto our postmortem/fix list.", "text_chars": 1855, "code_blocks": 1, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": ["GCE_DON\\command-center\\cable-car\\transport\\realDriveClient.js"], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "9547528b-7adc-4540-a707-4009fc8c326c", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790398238.359, "updated_at": 1790398258.182264, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "yeah why is this happeneing twice now it worked once", "text_chars": 52, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "3cb54032-78fa-42f6-9db7-2047bc2dddab", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790398245.578954, "updated_at": 1790398245.578954, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "887642a9-6dfd-4be7-a440-28dec653a6de", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790398245.582571, "updated_at": 1790398257.601802, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Because the thing that “worked once” was **not yet encoded as a durable startup capability**. It worked because Nico, in that specific session, was explicitly told how to do it and then proved the path.\n\nWhat happened twice is the same underlying gap:\n\n- The model starts fresh.\n- Its bootstrap tells it the **seat role**, session controls, routing, authority, etc.\n- But it does **not yet carry a deterministic “how to retrieve Drive artifacts from this machine” contract**.\n- So the model inspects its immediate runtime, sees no mounted Drive and no obvious direct Drive tool, and concludes: “Drive is unreachable.”\n- Then it correctly stops instead of inventing.\n\nThe one time it worked, Nico had already been given the surgical correction and discovered/proved this path:\n\n`GCE_DON\\command-center\\cable-car\\transport\\realDriveClient.js`\n\nwith authenticated OAuth and direct export by Drive ID.\n\nThat knowledge lived in **that session’s working state**, not in the reusable bootstrap/runtime contract. So when another model/seat/session starts, it has no reason to know that path exists unless we explicitly give it again.\n\nSo this is **not really a model problem**. It is a framework plumbing omission:\n\n> We have transport capability, but we have not yet made transport discovery deterministic at bootstrap.\n\nThe fix is straightforward: every relevant bootstrap should carry a tiny capability-resolution block that says, in effect:\n\n> For Google Drive artifacts, do not use WebFetch, do not require a mounted Drive, and do not assume Drive is unavailable. First resolve the authenticated Cable Car Drive client and retrieve by Drive ID/name. Only declare Drive unavailable if that authenticated path fails.\n\nThat would have prevented both of these stops.\n\nAnd this is exactly why your principle **“models execute; Framework carries continuity”** matters. Right now the Framework carries the seat identity well, but it still does not fully carry the **machine capability map**. That’s the missing p